  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nessler's reagent is an aqueous solution of potassium iodide, mercuric chloride, and potassium hydroxide. Its chemical formula is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>HgI</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>. It is used to detect the presence of ammonia. It turns into a pale brown colour in the presence of ammonia.</p><p>Nessler’s Reagent Reaction:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><munder><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>HgI</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>Nessler</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo> </mo><mi>reagent</mi></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>KOH</mi><mover><mo>→</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><munder><munder><mrow><mi>HgO</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>Hg</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></mrow><mo>⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>Iodide</mi><mo> </mo><mi>of</mi><mo> </mo><mi>Millon</mi><mo>'</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo> </mo><mi>base</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>brown</mi><mo> </mo><mi>precipitate</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></munder><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>KI</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>"
  }
